{"vid":"m7e1DLvJBvQ","source":"m7e1DLvJBvQ.en-US.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":1.3,"txt":"A Distributed Control System, or DCS,"},{"t":4.6,"txt":"is a system that is designed to control complex industrial processes."},{"t":9.5,"txt":"In this video, I’ll explain what a DCS is,"},{"t":13,"txt":"What a DCS is and why it’s used in the process industry,"},{"t":16,"txt":"The main components that make up a DCS,"},{"t":19,"txt":"and The key differences between a DCS and a PLC control system"},{"t":24.5,"txt":"Let’s start with a quick recap on process control."},{"t":28.3,"txt":"A Process is the transformation of raw materials into end products"},{"t":33.4,"txt":"through operations like mixing, heating, cooling, filtering, and storing."},{"t":39.3,"txt":"These raw materials are typically in liquid, gas, or slurry form,"},{"t":44.1,"txt":"and they travel through pipes to specifically engineered vessels"},{"t":47.7,"txt":"where operations are carried out."},{"t":50.2,"txt":"A process is monitored by instrumentation."},{"t":53.7,"txt":"These are sensors that check temperatures,"},{"t":56.1,"txt":"pressures, flow rates, and other important variables"},{"t":60,"txt":"to verify that the conditions are correct for the process to work as designed."},{"t":65,"txt":"Process control involves maintaining setpoints for process variables."},{"t":69.9,"txt":"If any of the sensors detect a deviation from a setpoint,"},{"t":73.5,"txt":"then a process controller responds"},{"t":75.8,"txt":"by adjusting actuators like pumps, valves, and heaters"},{"t":80.4,"txt":"to bring conditions back to the required range."},{"t":83.9,"txt":"Modern industrial processes are controlled by a Distributed Control System, or DCS."},{"t":90.3,"txt":"A DCS is an integrated system, made up of hardware and software components,"},{"t":96,"txt":"with characterized performance."},{"t":98.5,"txt":"The main components that make up a DCS are:"},{"t":102.1,"txt":"Instrumentation and I/O,"},{"t":104.6,"txt":"Controllers,"},{"t":106.1,"txt":"A centralized tag database,"},{"t":108.6,"txt":"Workstations,"},{"t":110.3,"txt":"Redundant hardware,"},{"t":112.1,"txt":"and A historian"},{"t":113.9,"txt":"Let’s look at each of these components in more detail."},{"t":117.3,"txt":"Field devices like sensors and actuators"},{"t":120.2,"txt":"connect back to controllers using hardwired connections"},{"t":123.7,"txt":"and industrial networks."},{"t":125.8,"txt":"Modern instrumentation devices often do more than sending a single process variable"},{"t":130.9,"txt":"back to a controller."},{"t":132.6,"txt":"They also send diagnostic data that helps operators to detect equipment issues"},{"t":137.5,"txt":"before they become failures."},{"t":139.9,"txt":"DCS controllers are responsible for running control strategies."},{"t":144.8,"txt":"Typically, these strategies are executed at consistent periodic intervals."},{"t":150,"txt":"In the process industry, most control strategies are built from a standardized library"},{"t":155.6,"txt":"of predefined function blocks."},{"t":157.9,"txt":"This library approach speeds up the engineering process and reduces the risk of"},{"t":163.3,"txt":"errors in a project."},{"t":165.5,"txt":"Although controllers are distributed across the plant,"},{"t":169,"txt":"all data is stored in a centralized tag database."},{"t":173.3,"txt":"This database acts as a single source of truth for every piece of data in the system."},{"t":179,"txt":"This tag database can be accessed by workstations on the network for monitoring"},{"t":183.8,"txt":"and troubleshooting."},{"t":185.9,"txt":"Operators, engineers, and technicians interact with the DCS through workstations."},{"t":192.3,"txt":"These workstations provide a real-time window into the process."},{"t":196.6,"txt":"Typically, workstations include standardized alarm management screens,"},{"t":201.1,"txt":"the ability to navigate between screens for different process areas,"},{"t":205.1,"txt":"and faceplates that let operators monitor and control individual DCS components."},{"t":211.2,"txt":"Some common tasks carried out with faceplates include changing setpoints,"},{"t":216.3,"txt":"switching between automatic and manual control of a loop, and acknowledging an alarm."},{"t":222.1,"txt":"RealPars Business helps engineers, technicians, and operators"},{"t":226.2,"txt":"build the practical skills needed to work with systems like these."},{"t":230.4,"txt":"Learn more at RealPars.com/Business."},{"t":234.8,"txt":"Some processes are so critical that they cannot stop even if a fault occurs."},{"t":240.5,"txt":"For example, an uplanned shutdown of a refinery"},{"t":243.9,"txt":"can cost hundreds of thousands of dollars per hour."},{"t":247.6,"txt":"To ensure that a process can continue to run even if a fault occurs,"},{"t":252.2,"txt":"many DCSes are built with redundant hardware including redundant controllers,"},{"t":257.5,"txt":"redundant power supplies, and redundant network configurations."},{"t":262.5,"txt":"By leveraging redundant hardware, plants can ensure that a single fault"},{"t":267,"txt":"won’t cause the whole process to stop."},{"t":270.1,"txt":"Finally, a DCS generally includes a historian."},{"t":274.3,"txt":"A historian is a time-series database that records tag values over time."},{"t":279.9,"txt":"This data can be recalled for product quality tracking, safety audits,"},{"t":284.8,"txt":"process optimization, and regulatory reporting."},{"t":288.9,"txt":"Now that you understand how a DCS is structured, it is useful to compare a DCS"},{"t":294.6,"txt":"to a PLC control system."},{"t":297.2,"txt":"A PLC control system is typically used for high-speed, discrete, repetitive,"},{"t":303.3,"txt":"and deterministic control."},{"t":305.6,"txt":"Think of an automotive assembly line where there is a fixed sequence"},{"t":309.3,"txt":"that involves turning outputs on or off,"},{"t":312.1,"txt":"and the control needs to execute in precise, predictable cycles."},{"t":316.6,"txt":"A PLC system is built up from components based on an application’s requirements."},{"t":322.3,"txt":"An engineer selects a processor, IO modules, network equipment, and an HMI"},{"t":329,"txt":"and integrates them into a working system."},{"t":332,"txt":"PLCs are typically programmed using the Ladder Diagram programming language."},{"t":337.3,"txt":"A DCS is designed for the complex analog control"},{"t":341.2,"txt":"that is required to keep continuous or batch processes under control."},{"t":346.4,"txt":"Since they are used for continuous and batch processes"},{"t":349.8,"txt":"they are typically found in chemical manufacturing,"},{"t":352.8,"txt":"pharmaceutical manufacturing, and oil and gas refineries."},{"t":357.4,"txt":"In these environments, the control system needs to monitor analog variables"},{"t":362.1,"txt":"like temperature, flow, and pressure"},{"t":365.4,"txt":"and control hundreds or thousands of control loops simultaneously."},{"t":370.6,"txt":"Because a DCS needs to have precise, characterized performance,"},{"t":375.3,"txt":"it is purchased as a complete system from a single vendor."},{"t":379.7,"txt":"Rather than programming in Ladder Diagram, engineers configured DCS control strategies"},{"t":385.8,"txt":"using a library of function blocks that allow fast, repeatable,"},{"t":390.4,"txt":"and precise engineering of a system."},{"t":393.4,"txt":"Now you know what a Distributed Control System is."},{"t":397,"txt":"Specifically, you learned:"},{"t":399.1,"txt":"What process control is"},{"t":400.9,"txt":"and why a DCS is used for process control,"},{"t":404.7,"txt":"The main components that make up a DCS,"},{"t":407.8,"txt":"and The differences between a DCS and PLC control system"},{"t":412.6,"txt":"PlantPAx, Rockwell Automation’s DCS, is implemented using Logix 5000 PLCs."},{"t":420.2,"txt":"If you want to take the next step and learn how to program Logix 5000 PLCs,"},{"t":425.4,"txt":"check out our Learn Logix series of courses."},{"t":429.3,"txt":"RealPars members get access to the LearnLogix series and all of our other"},{"t":434.2,"txt":"great courses on industrial automation."},{"t":437.4,"txt":"Learn more at RealPars.com/Business"},{"t":441.2,"txt":"or using the link in the description below this video."}],"words":[{"t":1.28,"w":"A"},{"t":1.28,"w":"Distributed"},{"t":1.28,"w":"Control"},{"t":1.28,"w":"System,"},{"t":1.28,"w":"or"},{"t":1.28,"w":"DCS,"},{"t":4.585,"w":"is"},{"t":4.585,"w":"a"},{"t":4.585,"w":"system"},{"t":4.585,"w":"that"},{"t":4.585,"w":"is"},{"t":4.585,"w":"designed"},{"t":4.585,"w":"to"},{"t":4.585,"w":"control"},{"t":4.585,"w":"complex"},{"t":4.585,"w":"industrial"},{"t":4.585,"w":"processes."},{"t":9.452,"w":"In"},{"t":9.452,"w":"this"},{"t":9.452,"w":"video,"},{"t":9.452,"w":"I’ll"},{"t":9.452,"w":"explain"},{"t":9.452,"w":"what"},{"t":9.452,"w":"a"},{"t":9.452,"w":"DCS"},{"t":9.452,"w":"is,"},{"t":12.978,"w":"What"},{"t":12.978,"w":"a"},{"t":12.978,"w":"DCS"},{"t":12.978,"w":"is"},{"t":12.978,"w":"and"},{"t":12.978,"w":"why"},{"t":12.978,"w":"it’s"},{"t":12.978,"w":"used"},{"t":12.978,"w":"in"},{"t":12.978,"w":"the"},{"t":12.978,"w":"process"},{"t":12.978,"w":"industry,"},{"t":15.97,"w":"The"},{"t":15.97,"w":"main"},{"t":15.97,"w":"components"},{"t":15.97,"w":"that"},{"t":15.97,"w":"make"},{"t":15.97,"w":"up"},{"t":15.97,"w":"a"},{"t":15.97,"w":"DCS,"},{"t":19.035,"w":"and"},{"t":19.035,"w":"The"},{"t":19.035,"w":"key"},{"t":19.035,"w":"differences"},{"t":19.035,"w":"between"},{"t":19.035,"w":"a"},{"t":19.035,"w":"DCS"},{"t":19.035,"w":"and"},{"t":19.035,"w":"a"},{"t":19.035,"w":"PLC"},{"t":19.035,"w":"control"},{"t":19.035,"w":"system"},{"t":24.498,"w":"Let’s"},{"t":24.498,"w":"start"},{"t":24.498,"w":"with"},{"t":24.498,"w":"a"},{"t":24.498,"w":"quick"},{"t":24.498,"w":"recap"},{"t":24.498,"w":"on"},{"t":24.498,"w":"process"},{"t":24.498,"w":"control."},{"t":28.327,"w":"A"},{"t":28.327,"w":"Process"},{"t":28.327,"w":"is"},{"t":28.327,"w":"the"},{"t":28.327,"w":"transformation"},{"t":28.327,"